rl-rollout-replay — NOTICE

This directory (apps/rl-rollout-replay/) is a CPU-only clear-experiment toy
inspired by:

  Sheng, Gu, Zeng, Zhou, Viel, Wang, Tajwar, Zanette,
  "Reinforcement Learning Can Be Recovered From Its Own Rollouts",
  arXiv:2611.33102 (2026)
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.33102
  https://arxiv.org/html/2611.33102v2

Found via a bookmarked X post by @rosinality. The post was not fetched.
Claims used here were checked on the arXiv HTML (v2), not on the post.

The HTML does not link an official code repository. The paper says the
language-model runs were implemented in verl. verl is not vendored and was
not run. This directory is a clean-room reimplementation of the two replay
protocols on a tiny GRU: maximum-likelihood replay (token NLL on every
archived rollout) and naive replay of the REINFORCE update on the same
archive (paper Eq. 2). It is not a reproduction of the Qwen, SmolLM, maze,
or ImageNet experiments. Those numbers, when quoted in the README, are the
paper's.

No warranty. Research / demo use. Checkpoints and rollout archives stay in
work/ and are git-ignored.
